WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.243
RNA-protein interactions drive gene regulation,

00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:06.708
yet measuring them in the lab is slow and costly,

00:00:06.788 --> 00:00:11.303
and existing predictors lean on small,
protein-specific datasets.

00:00:11.383 --> 00:00:13.637
This work introduces RNAInterAct,

00:00:13.717 --> 00:00:19.293
a large curated dataset of non-coding RNA-protein
interactions, and RPIembeddor,

00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:26.363
a transformer model that classifies whether any RNA
and protein interact using only their sequences.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:29.828
By feeding embeddings from two foundation models,

00:00:29.908 --> 00:00:34.848
RNA-FM for RNA and ESM-2 for proteins, into an
attention-based network,

00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:43.120
RPIembeddor outperforms prior state-of-the-art
methods and generalizes to unseen RNA families and data distributions.
